IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-art8-address.l4: tests of Article 8(4), the principal address of a registered charity (src:239-242).
-- Expected values are decided from the text of the three limbs: (a) the registered office or business address; (b) the main premises in Jersey unless a private dwelling house;
-- (c) if neither applies, the address in Jersey of one of the governors (so, any one of them).

§ `Tests of Article 8(4): the principal address`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      jersey IS A BOOLEAN
      dwelling IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
`main premises at` a `in Jersey` jersey `a private dwelling house` dwelling MEANS
    `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))` WITH
        address IS a
        `in Jersey` IS jersey
        `a private dwelling house` IS dwelling
        `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity` IS TRUE

GIVEN law IS A BOOLEAN
      office IS A MAYBE STRING
      main IS A MAYBE `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
      governors IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
`address facts: Law requires an office` law `, office` office `, main premises` main `, governors' addresses` governors MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH
        `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS law
        `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS office
        `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS main
        `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS governors

`the shop` MEANS `main premises at` "5 Pier Road" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE
`the flat` MEANS `main premises at` "7 Elm Close" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` TRUE
`the London office` MEANS `main premises at` "5 Regent Street, London" `in Jersey` FALSE `a private dwelling house` FALSE
`two governors' addresses` MEANS LIST "3 Rue Bas", "4 Rue Haute"

`the company entity` MEANS `an entity falling within` (LIST `a company`)
`the foundation entity` MEANS `an entity falling within` (LIST `a foundation`)
`the unincorporated entity` MEANS `an entity falling within` (LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`)
`the enactment-incorporated entity` MEANS `an entity falling within` (LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`)

§§ `Limb (a): the registered office or business address`

-- A company whose constitutional Law requires a registered office in Jersey: that address, whatever the premises or the governors.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the company entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` TRUE `, office` (JUST "10 Library Place") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "10 Library Place"
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` fav `the company entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` TRUE `, office` (JUST "10 Library Place") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
-- "other entity required by its constitutional Law": a body incorporated under an enactment whose enactment requires an office in Jersey.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the enactment-incorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` TRUE `, office` (JUST "1 Broad Street") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "1 Broad Street"
-- The Law requires an office but none is given: the entity is within (a), which gives no address; (b) and (c) are not reached.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the company entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` TRUE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` fav `the company entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` TRUE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)

-- F3.9: a foundation whose constitutional Law (as an input) does not require an office or business address in Jersey, though one is given.
-- Favoured reading: not within (a), so (b): the main premises.  Other reading: every foundation is within (a), so the office.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4)(a) the registered charity is an entity within sub-paragraph (a)` fav `the foundation entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` (JUST "2 Bath Street") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the foundation entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` (JUST "2 Bath Street") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "5 Pier Road"
#ASSERT `Art 8(4)(a) the registered charity is an entity within sub-paragraph (a)` `interpretation F3.9 reading B` `the foundation entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` (JUST "2 Bath Street") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `interpretation F3.9 reading B` `the foundation entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` (JUST "2 Bath Street") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "2 Bath Street"
-- Likewise a company; on the other reading with no office given, there is no address.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `interpretation F3.9 reading B` `the company entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the company entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "5 Pier Road"
-- An unincorporated body is neither a company nor a foundation: the same on both readings.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4)(a) the registered charity is an entity within sub-paragraph (a)` `interpretation F3.9 reading B` `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
#ASSERT `Art 8(4)(a) the registered charity is an entity within sub-paragraph (a)` `interpretation F3.9 reading B` `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` TRUE `, office` (JUST "1 Broad Street") `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)

§§ `Limb (b): the main premises in Jersey, unless a private dwelling house`

#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "5 Pier Road"
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
-- The main premises are outside Jersey: (b) cannot give an address "in Jersey", so (c).
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the London office`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS `two governors' addresses`
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `interpretation F3.10 reading B` `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the London office`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS `two governors' addresses`
-- No main premises at all: (c).
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` NOTHING `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS `two governors' addresses`

§§ `Limb (c): the address in Jersey of one of the governors`

-- "One of the governors": any of them may be entered, so both addresses are allowed and nothing chooses between them.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the address is a principal address of the registered charity` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` NOTHING `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) "3 Rue Bas"
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the address is a principal address of the registered charity` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` NOTHING `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) "4 Rue Haute"
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4) the address is a principal address of the registered charity` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` NOTHING `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) "5 Pier Road"
-- No premises and no governor with an address in Jersey: no principal address.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` NOTHING `, governors' addresses` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` NOTHING `, governors' addresses` EMPTY)

§§ `F3.10: main premises that are a private dwelling house`

-- Favoured reading: the "unless" takes (b) away, so "neither (a) nor (b) applies" and (c) is reached.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the flat`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS `two governors' addresses`
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` fav `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the flat`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
-- Other reading: (b) applies to every entity not within (a) and gives no address for a private dwelling house, so the charity has none.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `interpretation F3.10 reading B` `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the flat`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` `interpretation F3.10 reading B` `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the flat`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`)
-- Not disturbed where the premises are not a dwelling house.
#ASSERT `Art 8(4) the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` `interpretation F3.10 reading B` `the unincorporated entity` (`address facts: Law requires an office` FALSE `, office` NOTHING `, main premises` (JUST `the shop`) `, governors' addresses` `two governors' addresses`) EQUALS LIST "5 Pier Road"
